{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>פני הצאן אל עקד.</b> The reason he did not say ״אל נקד״ or ״אל טלוא״ — perhaps it is because the flock would be more aroused by this type than by the other two." "<b>וישת לו עדרים וגו׳.</b> He intended by this that the flock would always look only at those types and not at other types, for in this way they would not give birth at all except to that same type — for otherwise Jacob would need to give some of his sheep to Laban when they gave birth to a type that is not עקד and טלוא, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:07.538259181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}